;; Exemptions for `bb check:isolation`.
;;
;; Every entry is a library that loads a namespace it does not declare. Two
;; kinds live here, and the :why says which:
;;
;;   TO FIX  — works in the monorepo and throws for anyone who takes the library
;;             off Clojars. Has a ticket.
;;   BY DESIGN — deliberate late binding for an optional companion library. The
;;             call site carries the same reason inline, and the feature
;;             degrades rather than failing when the companion is absent.
;;
;; An entry that stops exempting anything fails the build either way, so neither
;; kind can quietly outlive its reason.
;;
;; Every entry MUST carry a `:why`. The gate rejects one without it rather than
;; honouring it: an exemption with no stated reason cannot be burnt down, and is
;; indistinguishable from an unfixed bug (BOU-250). An entry that stops exempting
;; anything also fails the build — left in place it is a pre-approval for the
;; next regression of the same shape.
;;
;; Before adding an entry, the alternatives are usually right:
;;
;;   * Declare the dependency in the library's deps.edn, as
;;     `wagoe/<lib> {:local/root "../<lib>"}`. Honest, and correct whenever the
;;     coupling is real and wanted.
;;   * Invert it behind a port the application wires up. Correct when the
;;     library should not carry the weight of the other one — realtime should
;;     not drag in auth, MFA and persistence to verify a token.
;;
;; `:namespace :any` exempts a library's whole surface. It is for a library
;; whose runtime is not the JVM, not for one with a lot of work outstanding.

{:allow
 [;; ==========================================================================
  ;; BOU-307 — the remaining dynamic-resolve sites
  ;; ==========================================================================
  ;; Real cross-library coupling, dynamically loaded, none of it declared. Each
  ;; needs the same decision: declare it, or invert it behind a port.
  {:lib "email"     :namespace "wagoe.jobs.ports"
   :why "BY DESIGN. Optional companion: email sends synchronously when no job
         queue is wired, and enqueues when one is. Declaring wagoe/jobs would
         make a queue mandatory for anyone sending mail. Documented at both call
         sites in jobs_integration.clj."}
  {:lib "reports"   :namespace "wagoe.jobs.ports"
   :why "BY DESIGN. Same optional-companion shape as email's."}
  {:lib "workflow"  :namespace "wagoe.jobs.ports"
   :why "BY DESIGN. Same optional-companion shape as email's."}
  {:lib "workflow"  :namespace "wagoe.jobs.core.job"
   :why "TO FIX. BOU-307 follow-up. Optional-companion binding like the others, but it
         reaches past the jobs ports into its core — a layering question on top of
         the dependency one. jobs should expose what workflow needs on its port."}

  {:lib "platform"  :namespace "wagoe.devtools.shell.dashboard.middleware"
   :why "BY DESIGN. Dev-only: the branch is behind (= :dev profile) and degrades to no
         enrichment when devtools is absent. Documented inline in routes.clj."}
  {:lib "platform"  :namespace "wagoe.i18n.shell.middleware"
   :why "TO FIX. BOU-131 deprecation path — the call site logs that wiring :i18n here is
         deprecated and builds the middleware anyway. Clears when that argument goes."}

  ;; ==========================================================================
  ;; test-support — application test scaffolding
  ;; ==========================================================================
  {:lib "platform"  :namespace "wagoe.test-support.shell.handler"
   :why "TO FIX. Loads an application namespace that ships in no library — the same shape
         wagoe.config had before BOU-306. Survivable only because the branch is
         behind a flag that throws outside :test and :dev."}
  {:lib "platform"  :namespace "wagoe.test-support.shell.reset"
   :why "TO FIX. Same as the test-support handler above."}]}
